  "id": "community-mental-health",
  "term": "community mental health",
  "definition": "Community mental health is support for people with mental health difficulties while they continue living in the community, rather than only in hospital settings. It commonly involves multidisciplinary outreach teams that provide personalized help such as managing symptoms, supporting families, assisting with daily living, linking people with medical and social services, and helping with crises, work, education, or relationships.",
